Hi,
As a last resort, I hope someone in this group will be able to shed some light on issues I've been having while trying to build/run a SEM using lavaan.

The problem: lavaan keeps throwing more and more errors including...
-------------------------
Warning message: In lav_samplestats_from_data(lavdata = lavdata, missing = lavoptions$missing, : lavaan WARNING: sample covariance can not be inverted

Warning message: In lav_data_full(data = data, group = group, group.label = group.label, : lavaan WARNING: unordered factor(s) with more than 2 levels detected in data: BugTreat

Error in fitMeasures(object, fit.measures = "default") : object 'logl.H1' not found
-------------------------

The sample covariance error was the first one to show up, and is the one I've been trying to fix.  However, more and more errors are thrown, so I haven't even been able to address this.

I have included my code for a simple example model below. I have also included the data from dput().

--------------------
Abun2 <- read.csv("GzrAbun_SEM_MSIII_2009_DATA TO SHARE.csv", header=T)
names(Abun2)
str(Abun2)

#Examine the covariance matrix
Amat2 <- Abun2[,c(9:26)]
