On 07/02/2014 07:55 PM, rachael...@gmail.com wrote:
> Hi,
> As a last resort, I hope someone in this group will be able to shed some
> light on issues I've been having while trying to build/run a SEM using
> lavaan.
>
> The problem: lavaan keeps throwing more and more errors including...

> -------------------------
> Warning message: In lav_samplestats_from_data(lavdata = lavdata, missing
> = lavoptions$missing, : lavaan WARNING: sample covariance can not be
> inverted

Look at this:

 > cor(Abun2[,c("Sc201_Stock","Sc202_Stock","Sc203_Stock","Sc210_Stock")])
             Sc201_Stock Sc202_Stock Sc203_Stock Sc210_Stock
Sc201_Stock   1.0000000   0.9954023   0.9933993   0.9607689
Sc202_Stock   0.9954023   1.0000000   0.9998189   0.9829169
Sc203_Stock   0.9933993   0.9998189   1.0000000   0.9862414
Sc210_Stock   0.9607689   0.9829169   0.9862414   1.0000000

and then

 >
eigen(cor(Abun2[,c("Sc201_Stock","Sc202_Stock","Sc203_Stock","Sc210_Stock")]))$values
[1]  3.959383e+00  4.061738e-02 -9.020562e-17 -5.133578e-16

There is too much overlap among these 4 variables. You need to capture
the common information in one (two at the most) variables.

> Warning message: In lav_data_full(data = data, group = group,
> group.label = group.label, : lavaan WARNING: unordered factor(s) with
> more than 2 levels detected in data: BugTreat

BugTreat is a factor (with 3 levels). lavaan (unlike lm, glm) does not
automatically expand factors to a set of dummy variables. You have to do
that manually.

For example:

Abun2$BugTreat1 <- ifelse(Abun2$BugTreat == "Immigration", 1, 0)
Abun2$BugTreat2 <- ifelse(Abun2$BugTreat == "Initial", 1, 0)

and then you replace 'BugTreat' in your model syntax by those two dummy
variables:

modbb <- 'Sc200_FinalAbun ~ Sc200_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 +  TempTreat
            Sc201_FinalAbun ~ Sc201_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 +
TempTreat
            Sc202_FinalAbun ~ Sc202_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 +
TempTreat
            Sc203_FinalAbun ~ Sc203_Stock + BugTreat1 + BugTreat2 +

TempTreat
            Sc210_FinalAbun ~ Sc210_Stock +  TempTreat
            Sc211_FinalAbun ~ Sc211_Stock +  TempTreat '

This works, but you still have to deal with the *_Stock variables.

Yves.

