I did not see this with the model/data you posted.

The error is only triggered (in lavaan 0.5-16) if some columns in your
data.frame are of type 'matrix' (instead of numeric/integer/factor)...

If your data.frame is called 'Data', and the variables in your model are
(say), 'x1', 'x2', 'x3', type

varTable(Data[,c("x1","x2","x3")])

In the 'type' column: identify the variables that are of type 'matrix'.
And make them numeric. For example, if "x3" is of type matrix:

Data$x3 <- as.numeric(Data$x3)

Yves.

