> Hi Everyone,

I am new to R and new to Lavaan package. I am trying to perform SEM on a set of Binary variables. I have been using the same code and following the steps mentioned , but unfortunately i am facing this error continuously which is stopping me from doing further analysis . Can anyone help me pleaseeee.

My code:
require(foreign)
data<-read.spss("Aguila_Screened_Var.sav",use.value.labels=FALSE,to.data.frame=TRUE)
attach(data)
data1<-cbind(A1B1,A2B1,A3B1,A4B1,A5B1,A6B1,A7B1,A8B1,A9B1,A10B1)
HS.model<-'vis =~ A1B1+ A2B1+ A3B1
           tex =~ A4B1+ A5B1+ A6B1
           spe =~ A7B1+ A8B1+ A9B1'
fit<- cfa(HS.model,data=data1)

Error:
Error in file(file, "r") : cannot open the connection
In addition: Warning message:
In file(file, "r") : cannot open file 'vis =~ A1B1+ A2B1+ A3B1
           tex =~ A4B1+ A5B1+ A6B1
